From f907320e755721a39233720bf58e5d984abe20a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom de Vries <tdevries@suse.de>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:07:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] [gdb/testsuite] Handle help() timeout in
 gdb.python/python.exp

I ran into the following timeout in test-case gdb.python/python.exp:
...
(gdb) python
>help()
>end
FAIL: $exp: python interactive help: python; help(); end (timeout)
define zzq
Welcome to Python 3.13's help utility! If this is your first time using
Python, you should definitely check out the tutorial at
https://docs.python.org/3.13/tutorial/.

Enter the name of any module, keyword, or topic to get help on writing
Python programs and using Python modules.  To get a list of available
modules, keywords, symbols, or topics, enter "modules", "keywords",
"symbols", or "topics".

Each module also comes with a one-line summary of what it does; to list
the modules whose name or summary contain a given string such as "spam",
enter "modules spam".

To quit this help utility and return to the interpreter,
enter "q", "quit" or "exit".

help> No Python documentation found for 'define zzq'.
...

The timeout means that gdb is stuck at the "help>" prompt, making all the
following tests fail.

Fix this using a clean_restart.
---
 gdb/testsuite/gdb.python/python.exp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gdb/testsuite/gdb.python/python.exp b/gdb/testsuite/gdb.python/python.exp
index 96977dff629..f5be68e0f22 100644
--- a/gdb/testsuite/gdb.python/python.exp
+++ b/gdb/testsuite/gdb.python/python.exp
@@ -74,6 +74,10 @@ with_test_prefix "python interactive help" {
     }
 }
 
+# A timeout in the previous test would have gdb stuck at the "help>" prompt,
+# causing all following tests to fail.  Start a clean session.
+clean_restart
+
 gdb_test_multiline "show python command" \
   "define zzq" "Type commands for definition of .* just \"end\"\\.*" \
   "python" "" \
-- 
2.51.0

